\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{1}{4}{Pipeline architecture of \clax and \claxpt . The shared backbone (top row) computes background cosmology, recombination, and the Einstein--Boltzmann perturbation hierarchy. Two branches produce CMB angular power spectra (left, via line-of-sight integration and lensing) and galaxy power spectrum multipoles (right, via one-loop EFT perturbation theory). Every module is independently validated against \class (\clax ) or \classpt (\claxpt ) reference data. The entire pipeline is end-to-end differentiable: \texttt {jax.grad} propagates exact reverse-mode gradients from any output back to \texttt {CosmoParams}}{figure.caption.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:pipeline@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][3][]4}{}{}{}}
\newlabel{tab:landscape}{{1}{4}{Comparison of cosmological theory codes. ``AD'' = automatic differentiation. ``PT'' = one-loop perturbation theory for galaxy clustering. \clax is the only code combining CMB $\Cl $, lensing, $\Pk $, and 1-loop PT with full AD on GPU}{table.caption.2}{}}
